    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d40-a1">

                <pb facs="0834" n="824" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv09/pg824"/>

                <head>Appendix A to HD–124</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Proposed Correction to Above Note to
                        Baron von Lersner</hi><anchor n="3" xml:id="d40-f1"/></p>
                <p>The last phrase of the text to the last line seems to imply that the maximum of
                    125,000 tons refers only to the reduction proposed by the experts after
                    verification.</p>
                <p>If the intention of the Supreme Council is to have this maximum cover the
                    reductions proposed for whatever the reason may be, that is to say, after
                    valuation or for economic reasons, it would seem advisable to suppress this
                    phrase, as the last phrase of the alinea, and to make a separate alinea reading
                    as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“In no case shall the total reduction exceed the amount of 125,000
                            tons.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Drafting Committee<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henri
                            Fromageot</hi></signed>
                    <lb/><dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1920-01-06"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >January</hi> 6, 1920</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
